Adapt RDO's rpm-master python-os-ken.spec to the released 2026.1 tarball
(os-ken 4.1.2, the version pinned by the 2026.1 upper-constraints).

os-ken 4.1.2 declares no console scripts at all - there is no [project.scripts]
in pyproject.toml and no console_scripts in setup.cfg - but the spec still
packages two of them:

    error: File not found: .../usr/bin/osken
    error: File not found: .../usr/bin/osken-manager

Neutron uses os-ken as a library (it is a BuildRequires and a runtime
dependency of openstack-neutron), never through those binaries, so dropping
them from %files costs nothing here.

diff -ur a/os-ken/python-os-ken.spec b/os-ken/python-os-ken.spec
--- a/python-os-ken.spec	2026-09-28 22:19:00
+++ b/python-os-ken.spec	2026-09-28 22:53:34
@@ -113,8 +113,6 @@
 %license LICENSE
 %{python3_sitelib}/%{srcname}
 %{python3_sitelib}/%{srcname}-*.dist-info
-%{_bindir}/%{binname}
-%{_bindir}/%{binname}-manager
 %dir %{_sysconfdir}/%{srcname}
 %config(noreplace) %attr(0644, root, neutron) %{_sysconfdir}/%{srcname}/%{srcname}.conf
 
